{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014oKqDpKrFYUWncjHaQQiTC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Fannan round 13 panel review — merged, deduplicated\n2\tHead reviewed: **f9a8d7e** (mimar-r4-fixes, PR #1), fresh GitHub clone at /workspace/panel-r13/fannan (left unmodified). Scope: `git diff d8408d4..f9a8d7e`, reviews/MIMAR-R12-changes-eb048fc.md, reviews/panel-r12/MERGED.md, then new issues. Times: Gaza (UTC+3), Oct 18 2026.\n3\tReviewers: Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`, Claude Code `claude -p`, Read/Grep/Glob only, cwd = clone) and GPT-6.1-Sol (Codex 0.163.0 `codex-dce exec -s read-only`, high reasoning). Grok CLI retested 5:12 AM: `API error (status 402 Payment Required): Grok Build usage balance exhausted` (not included).\n4\tRound 1: 5:12 AM to 5:18 AM (GPT) / 5:20 AM (Opus). Cross-check: 5:23 AM to 5:25 AM (both). No call stalled; nothing killed.\n5\tSeverity \"Opus / GPT\" = each reviewer's view after the cross-check. Browser reproduction is UNVERIFIED for every item (code reading, mock-DOM, VM or in-memory runs only).\n6\t\n7\t## Round-12 items (M01-M21) status\n8\t- Reported partial/incomplete: M01 (N02), M02 (N01), M03 (N04, N05, N21), M04 (N08, N09), M05 (N07), M06 (N11, N12), M07 (N06), M08 (N13, N14), M10 (N15), M11 (N03, N16), M12 (N10), M13 (N17, N18), M17 (N19), M20 (N20; also disputed D1), M21 (N14).\n9\t- No finding raised against M09, M14, M15, M16, M18 or the M19 closure. (Neither reviewer listed them, which isn't the same as a positive sign-off.)\n10\t\n11\t## Agreed open (confirmed by both)\n12\t| N | Source IDs | Opus / GPT | file:line | Problem | Fix |\n13\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n14\t| N01 | OPUS-01, GPT-02 | P1 / P1 | release/tools/width-screen.mjs:38,57,65-69 | M02 partial, new regression: under `body{overflow-x:hidden}`, `scrollerOf` returns body, so `offscreenLeft` is skipped, `beyond` excludes body and `unreachable` needs auto/scroll → `<p style=\"margin-left:-400px\">` or a left translate passes at every width (GPT mock: all failure arrays empty). | Don't treat a propagated body/html as a scroller, or measure body against the viewport `[0, innerWidth]` on both edges. Chrome regressions: negative margin and transform at 1440 and 320. |\n15\t| N02 | OPUS-02, GPT-01 | P1 / P1 | width-screen.mjs:22,32,52,84,88 | M01 partial: `shown` needs a positive element box and treats any ≤1×1 box as sr-only even with `overflow:visible` → nowrap text in a `display:contents` element, a 0×0 inline-block, or a `height:0` heading pushed left is skipped by the main loop, `inside` and the `unmeasured` fail-closed check (GPT mock: 900px text in a 320px scroller, no finding). | Decide visibility from computed style plus text-range rects. Count sr-only only when the box also clips. Regressions for `display:contents`, 0×0 nowrap and height:0 pushed left. |\n16\t| N03 | OPUS-03 (GPT MODIFY) | P2 / P2 | width-screen.mjs:48,54,60,76 | M11 partial: `beyond` uses `e.contains(d)`, which doesn't cross shadow boundaries; a shadow-only host also has empty light-DOM `textContent` and is skipped before clipping → shadow text cut off by a hidden host is neither `clipped` nor `offscreenLeft`. | Use composed ancestry (`within`) **and** composed text detection. Browser regression. |\n17\t| N04 | OPUS-04 | P2 / P2 | design-probe.mjs:52,59; pre-handoff-check.mjs:123; width-screen.mjs:72 | M03 selector gap: only `iframe, frame` count; `<object type=text/html>`, `<embed>`, `<fencedframe>` create nested documents that no probe/axe/reflow covers and that never reach `checks.frames`. | Count every nested browsing context (object, embed, fencedframe, portal) in `frames`/`unscannedScopes`. HTML `<object>` regression. |\n18\t| N05 | OPUS-05 (GPT MODIFY) | P2 / P2 | release/tests/design-probe.test.mjs:213-225; local-fixture.mjs:110,118-121 | The M03 frames gate is tested only by source regex/wiring; `framesCheck` never runs in a checker run. The fixture has no negative run for frames or spacing exceptions. VERIFICATION.md:21 \"frames PASS\" holds only because the fixture has no frame. (GPT: the spacing-exception resolver *does* have unit tests at spacing-scale.test.mjs:195-202; what's missing is integration.) | Executed fixture runs: same-origin srcdoc iframe → `checks.frames` FAIL at handoff / DEFERRED in wireframe; spacing exception without approver → FAIL, with a matching entry → PASS. |\n19\t| N06 | GPT-15 | P3 / P2 | reviews/MIMAR-R12-changes-eb048fc.md:5; test-results/r12/R12-M06-M08-M13-M17-M21-integrity-before.log:6; integrity.test.mjs:86-87 | **Untested claim stated as tested:** the record claims a behavioural before/after for every item, but the integrity \"before\" log stops at `SyntaxError … does not provide an export named 'VECTOR'` before any assertion ran. M07's negative coverage is a source regex only. | Label module-load failures as \"not behavioural\". Add a checker fixture where only a non-positional state has an integrity mismatch and assert that state fails. Correct the record. |\n20\t| N07 | OPUS-06 | P2 / P2 | design-probe.mjs:47; pre-handoff-check.mjs:86-88 | M05 partial: unreadable ordinary sheets are silently ignored (`try{…}catch{}`). Playwright `route('**/*')` doesn't see `data:` URLs, so `<link href=\"data:text/css;base64,…\">` carrying `html{-webkit-backdrop-filter:…}` escapes the served-file scan, CSSOM and computed checks (Safari renders it). Data-URL bypass UNVERIFIED. | Fail closed on any stylesheet (incl. `@import`) that wasn't served+scanned or can't be read. Refuse `data:`/`blob:` stylesheet URLs at handoff. Base64 regression. |\n21\t| N08 | OPUS-07 | P2 / P2 | design-probe.mjs:81-84 | M04 partial: only CSS escapes are decoded; JS `\\x2d`, `\\u002D`, `\\u{2d}` and escaped identifier letters in served JS are not (GPT executed: all returned false), e.g. `setProperty('-webkit-backdrop\\x2dfilter',…)`, `style.webkitBackdrop\\u0046ilter`. | For non-CSS kinds, decode JS escapes before matching; keep CSS handling separate. Regress each form. |\n22\t| N09 | GPT-03 | P2 / P1 | design-probe.mjs:81 | M04 partial: CSS comment stripping `/\\/\\*[\\s\\S]*?\\*\\//g` also runs on JS, so `const a=\"/*\"; el.style.webkitBackdropFilter=\"blur(4px)\"; const b=\"*/\";` returns false (GPT executed; valid JS). | For non-CSS kinds, match both raw and stripped text and fail if either matches (or use language-aware comment handling). Regression with quoted delimiters. |\n23\t| N10 | OPUS-08, GPT-10 | P2 / P2 | scripts/package-r3.py:42,51 | M12 partial: credential stems match only at the start of a path part, and plural `tokens` is allowed with any suffix. GPT executed: `aws-credentials.json`, `client-secret.json`, `client_secrets.json`, `api-token.json`, `github_token.txt`, `prod.secrets.json`, `oauth-tokens.json`, `tokens.production.json`, `tokens.backup.txt` all allowed. | Match stems anywhere at `[._-]` boundaries, plural included. Allow `tokens.json` only per q2 below. Keep the `secret-scan.json` and `token-references.mjs` allowances. Temp-tree tests for inputs and changed paths. |\n24\t| N11 | GPT-04, OPUS-10 | P2 / P2 | integrity.mjs:83; pre-handoff-check.mjs:171-173 | M06 partial: `VECTOR` omits accent ratios (`accentRatio`, `maxViewportAccent`), `filler`, `ruleOfThree`, frames/`unscannedFrames` and `unscannedScopes`; `sum('clipped')` etc. drop width identity, so {1440:1, 320:0} vs {1440:0, 320:1} compare equal. (GPT: lang/dir are already compared via `contentProbe`; Opus's claim otherwise is withdrawn.) | Compare a canonical gate-result structure including the omitted fields, with results keyed by width. Regress ratio-only, copy-signal-only and width-swapped differences. |\n25\t| N12 | GPT-05 | P3 / P2 | integrity.mjs:58; pre-handoff-check.mjs:173 | M06 partial: only `contrastFailures` survives; `contrastUnknown`/`contrastChecked` are dropped, so gradient-backed text (failures 0, unknown 1, checked 0) can give integrity PASS. (Opus: the main gate still fails axe `incomplete`, so only the diagnostic is affected.) | Keep `contrastUnknown`/`contrastChecked` in the vector; JS-off `checked===0` with probe `>0`, or required text unevaluated → INCOMPLETE. |\n26\t| N13 | GPT-06 | P2 / P1 | integrity.mjs:64 | M08 partial: content records hold slot IDs and h1 count only, no text; a JS-off skeleton with empty fixed-size slots looks equivalent (GPT mock). | Compare normalised visible text per slot and per heading, with counts. JS-populated skeleton regression must stay INCOMPLETE. |\n27\t| N14 | GPT-07 | P2 / P2 | integrity.mjs:110; integrity.test.mjs:69-70 | M08/M21: an explained `content` difference never sets `contentUnexplained`, so removing every slot and zeroing h1 still returns PASS with a reviewer entry (GPT executed; the test expects PASS). | Keep the reviewed waiver as evidence, but never PASS: GPT → INCOMPLETE/`pass:false`; Opus → a distinct `WAIVED-CONTENT` status with metrics unverified, listed in UNTESTED. Either way, update the test. |\n28\t| N15 | GPT-08 | P2 / P2 | width-screen.mjs:98 | M10 partial: `last.right >= extent.right - span` allows a full viewport of slack; a 340px table in a 320px scroller with one link at x=0-30 gets `keyboard:true`. | Require targets reaching both edges (`last.right >= extent.right-1`, `first.left <= extent.left+1`) or a focusable scroller. Narrow-overflow regression. |\n29\t| N16 | GPT-09 | P3 / P1 | width-screen.mjs:29; design-probe.mjs:43-44 | M11 partial: closed shadow roots vanish without an `unscannedScopes` record, so an internal sideways scroller in one is unmeasured (disclosed as untested, but not gated). | Count closed roots via CDP `DOM.getDocument({pierce:true})` and list them as unscanned scopes that fail at handoff. Regression. |\n30\t| N17 | GPT-11 | P2 / P2 | integrity.mjs:20-34,77 | M13 bypass: the rAF wrapper calls `native.call(window, cb)`, which looks up mutable `Function.prototype.call`; page code can patch it once, capture native rAF, restore it (GPT VM: 101 callbacks, counter stuck at 1, `rafLoopFrom` false). | Bind at init (`Function.prototype.call.bind(native)` or a captured `Reflect.apply`). Add `.call`/`.apply` to `nativeCheck`. Capture-and-restore regression. |\n31\t| N18 | GPT-12, OPUS-13 | P2 / P2 | pre-handoff-check.mjs:222-237 vs 254-267 | M13 incomplete: `rmState` never installs `rafCounterInit`, so a canvas/rAF loop on a declared state is unseen. (Opus also raises an about:blank child-frame rAF timing bypass, UNVERIFIED.) | One hardened reduced-motion routine for the page and every state. Regression: static page plus a state with a rAF loop. Test child-frame coverage separately. |\n32\t| N19 | GPT-13 | ENH / ENH | integrity.mjs:92 | M17 partial: `tamperSigns = []` default treats an omitted native-check result as PASS (the current caller passes null, so this affects the exported API only). | Drop the default; undefined/null → INCOMPLETE. Test. |\n33\t| N20 | OPUS-11, GPT-14 | P2 / P2 | spacing-scale.mjs:27; design-probe.mjs:6-10,64-72; pre-handoff-check.mjs:98-110 | M20/M11 gap: the spacing scan (and its exception registry), type sizes, centred/icon rows, placeholders (`body.innerText`), h1 and the copy TreeWalker skip open shadow roots, so off-scale spacing, lorem ipsum or unlisted copy there pass. | One composed-tree walker for spacingProbe, designProbe counters and copyProbe. Open-shadow regression per check. |\n34\t| N21 | OPUS-12 (GPT MODIFY) | P3 / P3 | release/UNTESTED.md:8,11,22; references/design-quality.md:34 | Docs contradict each other on frames: \"not inspected; a frame is a stop\" vs \"measured with … same-origin frames\" / cross-origin \"blocked\". The truth is partial glass/width inspection of readable frames, plus a mandatory frame FAIL. | Reword to \"partially inspected for glass/width, and every frame fails the handoff\". Mark the R11 wording superseded. Refresh hashes. |\n35\t\n36\t## Disputed — Mi'mar to decide\n37\t| D | Source | Opus | file:line | Opus's point | GPT's rejection |\n38\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n39\t| D1 | OPUS-09 | P2 | spacing-scale.mjs:40-42 | An approved `data-fannan-spacing-exception` excuses any off-scale value, negatives included, so `margin-left:-24px` passes. Fix: never excuse `px < 0`. | The owner rule (ASAD-PANEL-R5:52) refuses negative spacing **tokens**. token-references.mjs:7-16 and token-validation.test.mjs:168-176 deliberately allow negative margins, and scoped exceptions are allowed. A blanket negative-margin ban is a new rule. |\n40\t\n41\t## Panel questions\n42\t**q1 — fail on any frame?**\n43\t- Agreed, 2-0: keep the blanket frame stop for now (now including object/embed/fencedframe, N04). The target is protected recursive scanning of same-origin frames, with unreadable or unsupported frames failing. Switch only once every gate (axe, focus/target size, copy, contrast, spacing, integrity vector, reduced motion) runs inside each frame, because scanning for glass alone would turn \"not checked\" into PASS.\n44\t- Opus adds: real maps and video are usually cross-origin, so the resource boundary already stops them. The design deliverable should be a static poster/placeholder plus an engineering note.\n45\t- Split: Opus wants a scoped, role-reviewed `frameExceptions` entry (screen/state/lang, id, reason, qaGate/approver, manual a11y evidence) in the meantime. GPT says a scoped exception cannot substitute for missing coverage. Mi'mar to decide.\n46\t\n47\t**q2 — plural `tokens` exception?**\n48\t- Agreed, 2-0: **not safe as written**. Allow `tokens.json` only at the declared handoff token path **and** when its content validates as design tokens (DTCG leaves with `$value`; no `access_token`/`refresh_token`/`client_secret` keys). Refuse every other plural, suffixed, prefixed or infixed credential name.\n49\t- Opus adds a stdlib content screen for obvious secrets (`-----BEGIN`, `AKIA…`, `\"refresh_token\"`) on packaged files. GPT agrees it helps but says it can't replace the path+content boundary.\n50\t\n51\t## Verdicts\n52\t- Opus 5.5: round 1 `VERDICT: 13 ISSUES`; after cross-check `VERDICT: 22 ISSUES`.\n53\t- GPT-6.1-Sol: round 1 `VERDICT: 15 ISSUES`; after cross-check `VERDICT: 22 ISSUES`.\n54\t- Merged: 21 agreed (N01-N21) + 1 disputed (D1). Agreed P1 by both: N01, N02. Split P1/lower: N09, N13, N16. **Not zero issues.**\n55\t\n56\t## Cost\n57\tOpus (Claude Code `total_cost_usd`): round 1 $7.04 + cross-check $1.26 = **$8.30** (round 12: $14.39). GPT: no cost reported; tokens 140,126 (round 1) + 68,503 (cross-check). Grok: none (402).\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"808872f5-cb7c-4be7-8453-962e42cc3a49","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:24:00.035Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/reviews/panel-r13/MERGED.md","content":"# Fannan round 13 panel review — merged, deduplicated\nHead reviewed: **f9a8d7e** (mimar-r4-fixes, PR #1), fresh GitHub clone at /workspace/panel-r13/fannan (left unmodified). Scope: `git diff d8408d4..f9a8d7e`, reviews/MIMAR-R12-changes-eb048fc.md, reviews/panel-r12/MERGED.md, then new issues. Times: Gaza (UTC+3), Oct 18 2026.\nReviewers: Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`, Claude Code `claude -p`, Read/Grep/Glob only, cwd = clone) and GPT-6.1-Sol (Codex 0.163.0 `codex-dce exec -s read-only`, high reasoning). Grok CLI retested 5:12 AM: `API error (status 402 Payment Required): Grok Build usage balance exhausted` (not included).\nRound 1: 5:12 AM to 5:18 AM (GPT) / 5:20 AM (Opus). Cross-check: 5:23 AM to 5:25 AM (both). No call stalled; nothing killed.\nSeverity \"Opus / GPT\" = each reviewer's view after the cross-check. Browser reproduction is UNVERIFIED for every item (code reading, mock-DOM, VM or in-memory runs only).\n\n## Round-12 items (M01-M21) status\n- Reported partial/incomplete: M01 (N02), M02 (N01), M03 (N04, N05, N21), M04 (N08, N09), M05 (N07), M06 (N11, N12), M07 (N06), M08 (N13, N14), M10 (N15), M11 (N03, N16), M12 (N10), M13 (N17, N18), M17 (N19), M20 (N20; also disputed D1), M21 (N14).\n- No finding raised against M09, M14, M15, M16, M18 or the M19 closure. (Neither reviewer listed them, which isn't the same as a positive sign-off.)\n\n## Agreed open (confirmed by both)\n| N | Source IDs | Opus / GPT | file:line | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| N01 | OPUS-01, GPT-02 | P1 / P1 | release/tools/width-screen.mjs:38,57,65-69 | M02 partial, new regression: under `body{overflow-x:hidden}`, `scrollerOf` returns body, so `offscreenLeft` is skipped, `beyond` excludes body and `unreachable` needs auto/scroll → `<p style=\"margin-left:-400px\">` or a left translate passes at every width (GPT mock: all failure arrays empty). | Don't treat a propagated body/html as a scroller, or measure body against the viewport `[0, innerWidth]` on both edges. Chrome regressions: negative margin and transform at 1440 and 320. |\n| N02 | OPUS-02, GPT-01 | P1 / P1 | width-screen.mjs:22,32,52,84,88 | M01 partial: `shown` needs a positive element box and treats any ≤1×1 box as sr-only even with `overflow:visible` → nowrap text in a `display:contents` element, a 0×0 inline-block, or a `height:0` heading pushed left is skipped by the main loop, `inside` and the `unmeasured` fail-closed check (GPT mock: 900px text in a 320px scroller, no finding). | Decide visibility from computed style plus text-range rects. Count sr-only only when the box also clips. Regressions for `display:contents`, 0×0 nowrap and height:0 pushed left. |\n| N03 | OPUS-03 (GPT MODIFY) | P2 / P2 | width-screen.mjs:48,54,60,76 | M11 partial: `beyond` uses `e.contains(d)`, which doesn't cross shadow boundaries; a shadow-only host also has empty light-DOM `textContent` and is skipped before clipping → shadow text cut off by a hidden host is neither `clipped` nor `offscreenLeft`. | Use composed ancestry (`within`) **and** composed text detection. Browser regression. |\n| N04 | OPUS-04 | P2 / P2 | design-probe.mjs:52,59; pre-handoff-check.mjs:123; width-screen.mjs:72 | M03 selector gap: only `iframe, frame` count; `<object type=text/html>`, `<embed>`, `<fencedframe>` create nested documents that no probe/axe/reflow covers and that never reach `checks.frames`. | Count every nested browsing context (object, embed, fencedframe, portal) in `frames`/`unscannedScopes`. HTML `<object>` regression. |\n| N05 | OPUS-05 (GPT MODIFY) | P2 / P2 | release/tests/design-probe.test.mjs:213-225; local-fixture.mjs:110,118-121 | The M03 frames gate is tested only by source regex/wiring; `framesCheck` never runs in a checker run. The fixture has no negative run for frames or spacing exceptions. VERIFICATION.md:21 \"frames PASS\" holds only because the fixture has no frame. (GPT: the spacing-exception resolver *does* have unit tests at spacing-scale.test.mjs:195-202; what's missing is integration.) | Executed fixture runs: same-origin srcdoc iframe → `checks.frames` FAIL at handoff / DEFERRED in wireframe; spacing exception without approver → FAIL, with a matching entry → PASS. |\n| N06 | GPT-15 | P3 / P2 | reviews/MIMAR-R12-changes-eb048fc.md:5; test-results/r12/R12-M06-M08-M13-M17-M21-integrity-before.log:6; integrity.test.mjs:86-87 | **Untested claim stated as tested:** the record claims a behavioural before/after for every item, but the integrity \"before\" log stops at `SyntaxError … does not provide an export named 'VECTOR'` before any assertion ran. M07's negative coverage is a source regex only. | Label module-load failures as \"not behavioural\". Add a checker fixture where only a non-positional state has an integrity mismatch and assert that state fails. Correct the record. |\n| N07 | OPUS-06 | P2 / P2 | design-probe.mjs:47; pre-handoff-check.mjs:86-88 | M05 partial: unreadable ordinary sheets are silently ignored (`try{…}catch{}`). Playwright `route('**/*')` doesn't see `data:` URLs, so `<link href=\"data:text/css;base64,…\">` carrying `html{-webkit-backdrop-filter:…}` escapes the served-file scan, CSSOM and computed checks (Safari renders it). Data-URL bypass UNVERIFIED. | Fail closed on an