{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I'm verifying the body-propagation overflow logic, checking that the offscreen-left detection correctly handles cases where only the html element has hidden overflow and the documentElement is skipped as a scroller.\n\nI also need to check mixed cases, like when html and body have differing overflow settings, since one visible/one non-visible always computes to auto, and confirming scrollWidth still reflects actual content width even when overflow is hidden on the root.\n\nThen I'm checking edge cases: visibility collapse, clip-path inset detection for sr-only content, and how text rects are gathered for display:contents elements. I'm also verifying that transformed wrappers with offscreen children are still caught through their child text rects, and that right-side overflow clipping on the viewport still measures correctly via document scrollWidth.\n\nI move on to stepped-target logic sorted by left position, parentOf traversal through assigned slots for containment checks, and frame-related checks referenced in the pre-handoff validation script that I still need to inspect.\n\nNow I'm tracing how object/embed elements get treated as frames — an image object with no contentDocument counts as an unscanned frame, which fails closed safely, while a same-origin HTML object gets its scope pushed and visited like a normal frame. I need to check pre-handoff-check to see how it tallies frame scopes versus unscanned frames for the final pass/fail determination.\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_2012344f8fa749118ecdfd038ea4d0f0","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":17464,"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"9f6aabae-52c2-4785-9a56-d672d686281e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:24:22.727Z","thinking_duration_ms":13820,"thinking_display":"updates"}
