{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"I'm checking for edge cases in the stylesheet detection logic—confirming that data: URLs on link elements and @import rules still expose a usable href, and now considering whether cross-origin stylesheets could cause the served-set check to behave unexpectedly.\n\nThen I shift to whether Playwright's routing actually intercepts file:// URLs, since historically it may not, which would mean scanGlass never runs on served CSS from file-origin pages at all—and separately whether file:// stylesheets are treated as cross-origin due to each file being its own opaque origin, making cssRules throw unless already served.\n\nI also want to verify the rAF counter initialization script runs correctly in the main world and isn't something the page could tamper with, before moving on to checking the copy probe logic.\n\nChecking other edge cases now: zero-size glass elements with display:contents children, blocked stylesheet links failing the resource boundary check, and whether the state-page motion/integrity checks reuse the same served set correctly. Moving on to look at the N05 fixture tests and package-r3.py next.\n\n","type":"thinking"}],"id":"msg_95ba2605733548a0aad773b3878f9475","model":"claude-opus-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":17482,"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"7a7c2283-d286-4627-b778-d06f8b0f8be6","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:24:38.472Z","thinking_duration_ms":9018,"thinking_display":"updates"}
