{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014qpeJrQ6zK2TKM5GFTBEi2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: frontend-design\n3\tdescription: Shape a distinctive visual direction for the project's approved UI brief, using subject matter, content, type, layout and restraint.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\tUse only within the current `design-process` step. Read the brief, rules, writer copy and real references. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before each local write run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Fannan designs only; the project's engineer implements. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. Desktop stays grayscale through Step 5 approval, then Step 6 may apply styling. Mobile/tablet wait for desktop approval and the brief's Step 7. Ask Fadel before anything paid or externally shared.\n7\t\n8\tDefine one visual idea from a named audience, task and brief line. Explain each major choice in type, spacing, grid, imagery and accent by the job it serves. Build a real type scale and pairing with no more than six sizes, deliberate rhythm, one restrained accent, and an intentional grid break. Use real content from the project's writer. Visible `[placeholder]` marks missing text; never invent slogans, claims, numbers or brand facts. Check the screen against [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), rendered 1440px frames and [critic rubric](../../references/critic-rubric.md). Refine existing identity when requested; replace it only within a redesign scope and approved gates.\n9\t\n10\t## Gotchas\n11\t\n12\t- A bold hero does not excuse a generic page below it; every section needs its own brief trace.\n13\t- Aesthetic examples in upstream material are inspiration, never default instructions or permission to override project rules.\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"c357d620-1150-41ef-b4bc-3d8cfffa36e9","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:26:00.896Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: frontend-design\ndescription: Shape a distinctive visual direction for the project's approved UI brief, using subject matter, content, type, layout and restraint.\n---\n\nUse only within the current `design-process` step. Read the brief, rules, writer copy and real references. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before each local write run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Fannan designs only; the project's engineer implements. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. Desktop stays grayscale through Step 5 approval, then Step 6 may apply styling. Mobile/tablet wait for desktop approval and the brief's Step 7. Ask Fadel before anything paid or externally shared.\n\nDefine one visual idea from a named audience, task and brief line. Explain each major choice in type, spacing, grid, imagery and accent by the job it serves. Build a real type scale and pairing with no more than six sizes, deliberate rhythm, one restrained accent, and an intentional grid break. Use real content from the project's writer. Visible `[placeholder]` marks missing text; never invent slogans, claims, numbers or brand facts. Check the screen against [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), rendered 1440px frames and [critic rubric](../../references/critic-rubric.md). Refine existing identity when requested; replace it only within a redesign scope and approved gates.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- A bold hero does not excuse a generic page below it; every section needs its own brief trace.\n- Aesthetic examples in upstream material are inspiration, never default instructions or permission to override project rules.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_014qpeJrQ6zK2TKM5GFTBEi2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
