{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01W3rMMsV7Fyv1YHooqzFR2W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: a11y-wcag-audit\n3\tdescription: Audit a design prototype against WCAG 2.2 AA with automated and manual evidence for the engineer and QA gate.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\tRead the current project brief, settings, rules, languages and screen inventory. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before saving results run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). WCAG 2.2 AA is the minimum even if a project rule says less. Desktop stays first until its approval; a desktop audit does not approve mobile.\n7\t\n8\tRun available axe/Lighthouse and accessibility-tree checks on the rendered mock, then manually test keyboard traversal, focus visible and not obscured, focus order, target size, dragging alternatives, redundant entry, consistent help, errors, reduced motion/no-JS, page language and RTL/long-copy reflow. Record foreground/background contrast pairs, heading outline with one H1, standalone link/button names and intent for every image's alt text. For each issue record criterion, screen/state, element, evidence, severity, fix owner and retest result. Pass only with zero unresolved AA failures and complete manual evidence; unavailable checks are **untested** and block the Step 9 handoff. Give the project's engineer and QA gate actionable findings; do not edit source.\n9\t\n10\t## Gotchas\n11\t\n12\t- Automated zero violations does not cover focus behavior, language quality, meaningful labels or text clipping.\n13\t- Color must never be the only signal for a state; record a second cue.\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"c3802c63-2f47-412a-a777-1df1648a4db3","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:26:00.957Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/a11y-wcag-audit/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: a11y-wcag-audit\ndescription: Audit a design prototype against WCAG 2.2 AA with automated and manual evidence for the engineer and QA gate.\n---\n\nRead the current project brief, settings, rules, languages and screen inventory. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before saving results run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). WCAG 2.2 AA is the minimum even if a project rule says less. Desktop stays first until its approval; a desktop audit does not approve mobile.\n\nRun available axe/Lighthouse and accessibility-tree checks on the rendered mock, then manually test keyboard traversal, focus visible and not obscured, focus order, target size, dragging alternatives, redundant entry, consistent help, errors, reduced motion/no-JS, page language and RTL/long-copy reflow. Record foreground/background contrast pairs, heading outline with one H1, standalone link/button names and intent for every image's alt text. For each issue record criterion, screen/state, element, evidence, severity, fix owner and retest result. Pass only with zero unresolved AA failures and complete manual evidence; unavailable checks are **untested** and block the Step 9 handoff. Give the project's engineer and QA gate actionable findings; do not edit source.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- Automated zero violations does not cover focus behavior, language quality, meaningful labels or text clipping.\n- Color must never be the only signal for a state; record a second cue.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01W3rMMsV7Fyv1YHooqzFR2W","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01A1tuCWhfBz3xMvbUdBLG5p","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: manage-design-system\n3\tdescription: Retrieve, create or update a Stitch design system for a project whose settings explicitly choose Stitch.\n4\tallowed-tools:\n5\t  - \"stitch*:*\"\n6\t  - Read\n7\t  - web_fetch\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\tUse only after the current project's `design-tool:` selects Stitch, the pinned manifest is verified, and Step 5 desktop structure approval permits styling. Stitch is accessed through MCP with `STITCH_API_KEY` in the secret store. Read actual project/screen metadata and approved DESIGN.md, then show the proposed display name, color roles, fonts, roundness, affected screens and any cost. Wait for Fadel's written yes in Fannan's chat before upload, creation, application or any paid call. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. No shell uploader, direct key, CLI, repo edit or public link. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).\n11\t\n12\tUse `list_projects`, `list_screens`, `get_screen` and `list_design_systems` to ground the change. Have Fannan save and lint Google's DESIGN.md to zero errors in `/workspace/design-output/<project>/` after `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. For an approved upload, use `upload_design_md` MCP, then `create_design_system_from_design_md` with its returned selected screen instance. For applying an existing system, get screen instances from `get_project` and pass only `{id, sourceScreen}` in `selectedScreenInstances`; the asset ID comes from `list_design_systems`. Read [Stitch MCP shapes](references/stitch-mcp-shapes.md) for exact fields. Record result and affected version. Respect the project's brief-derived type/palette; do not substitute vendor defaults.\n13\t\n14\t## Gotchas\n15\t\n16\t- `selectedScreenInstances` with position or dimension fields can fail; use only the two required fields.\n17\t- An upload is a system change and needs its own explicit approval even if the design was approved.\n18\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"5bc9e65c-8d26-4caf-88b1-3ca3c4796eb8","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:26:00.959Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/manage-design-system/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: manage-design-system\ndescription: Retrieve, create or update a Stitch design system for a project whose settings explicitly choose Stitch.\nallowed-tools:\n  - \"stitch*:*\"\n  - Read\n  - web_fetch\n---\n\nUse only after the current project's `design-tool:` selects Stitch, the pinned manifest is verified, and Step 5 desktop structure approval permits styling. Stitch is accessed through MCP with `STITCH_API_KEY` in the secret store. Read actual project/screen metadata and approved DESIGN.md, then show the proposed display name, color roles, fonts, roundness, affected screens and any cost. Wait for Fadel's written yes in Fannan's chat before upload, creation, application or any paid call. WCAG 2.2 AA is the floor. No shell uploader, direct key, CLI, repo edit or public link. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md).\n\nUse `list_projects`, `list_screens`, `get_screen` and `list_design_systems` to ground the change. Have Fannan save and lint Google's DESIGN.md to zero errors in `/workspace/design-output/<project>/` after `$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. For an approved upload, use `upload_design_md` MCP, then `create_design_system_from_design_md` with its returned selected screen instance. For applying an existing system, get screen instances from `get_project` and pass only `{id, sourceScreen}` in `selectedScreenInstances`; the asset ID comes from `list_design_systems`. Read [Stitch MCP shapes](references/stitch-mcp-shapes.md) for exact fields. Record result and affected version. Respect the project's brief-derived type/palette; do not substitute vendor defaults.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- `selectedScreenInstances` with position or dimension fields can fail; use only the two required fields.\n- An upload is a system change and needs its own explicit approval even if the design was approved.\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01A1tuCWhfBz3xMvbUdBLG5p","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
