{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CEvd6sHKLShEC5XsH1BAJq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: design-canvas\n3\tdescription: Draw or review screens in the design tool named by the project's settings, preserving the current design stage and buildable states.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\tRead the brief, `settings.md`, `project-rules.md`, ui-map, writer copy and current step. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before every write run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Use only `design-tool:` from settings and its vendor skill; if unavailable, record the connection blocker. Never edit source code.\n7\t\n8\tAt Steps 4–5 draw 1440px **grayscale structure only**; wait for the recorded Step 5 approval before color/type styling. At Step 6 trace the single visual idea to brief lines, use [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), and name frames `<screen>/<state>/<version>`. Show default, hover, focus, disabled, empty, loading and error states; document language, direction, long-copy reflow and motion fallback. Preserve meaningful content and source-backed claims. In review mode, list evidence-backed copy, craft and WCAG 2.2 AA issues without altering source.\n9\t\n10\t## Gotchas\n11\t\n12\t- A vendor template or default palette never overrides the project's brief, approved wireframes or accessibility floor.\n13\t- External sharing, generation with cost, or a design-system mutation needs Fadel's yes in Fannan's chat.\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"d3abbf4b-2a6b-4004-8431-fe29cd6d7ee6","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:26:10.304Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/panel-r14/fannan/release/skills/design-canvas/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: design-canvas\ndescription: Draw or review screens in the design tool named by the project's settings, preserving the current design stage and buildable states.\n---\n\nRead the brief, `settings.md`, `project-rules.md`, ui-map, writer copy and current step. Verify the pinned manifest at session start; before every write run `\"$FANNAN_RELEASE/tools/readonly-precheck.sh\" \"/workspace/design-output/<project>/\" \"<project>\"`. See [security and install](../../references/security-and-install.md). Use only `design-tool:` from settings and its vendor skill; if unavailable, record the connection blocker. Never edit source code.\n\nAt Steps 4–5 draw 1440px **grayscale structure only**; wait for the recorded Step 5 approval before color/type styling. At Step 6 trace the single visual idea to brief lines, use [design quality](../../references/design-quality.md), and name frames `<screen>/<state>/<version>`. Show default, hover, focus, disabled, empty, loading and error states; document language, direction, long-copy reflow and motion fallback. Preserve meaningful content and source-backed claims. In review mode, list evidence-backed copy, craft and WCAG 2.2 AA issues without altering source.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- A vendor template or default palette never overrides the project's brief, approved wireframes or accessibility floor.\n- External sharing, generation with cost, or a design-system mutation needs Fadel's yes in Fannan's chat.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01CEvd6sHKLShEC5XsH1BAJq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
