{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013WDZxYWBux3pfZd6QGi9NQ","type":"tool_result","content":"release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:16:export const states = ['default', 'hover', 'focus', 'disabled', 'empty', 'loading', 'error'];\nrelease/skills/design-ui-map/SKILL.md:6:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/skills/design-process/SKILL.md:14:1. **Reconcile brief and success.** Map approved/open/evidence-pending decisions, page inventory, roles, gates, visitor tasks, measurable criteria. Resolve conflicts before exit.\nrelease/skills/design-connect/SKILL.md:10:- Connection success does not prove a vendor operation can run; verify capability only when the task needs it.\nrelease/references/security-and-install.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/references/security-and-install.md:47:3. **Stage inactive:** prepare the full new tree, dependencies outside it, approved pinned binary and its original launcher/support assets. Run integrity, syntax, regression, token, real-browser and negative-path checks. Require an actual successful end-to-end checker run with the protected binary on the target architecture. Validate every caller and each frontmatter name.\nrelease/references/security-and-install.md:50:6. **Verify before resuming:** read back names, memory, hashes and paths; run manifest verification, project prechecks, token build, checker and the existing thirteen helper tests if supplied. Any failure restores every changed member from the verified snapshot while execution stays held. Memory restoration must be proven too; a partial rollback is not success.\nrelease/references/security-and-install.md:65:| Resume | Explicit success after checks, or verified complete rollback on failure | Never automatically resume from an ambiguous or partially restored state |\nrelease/references/handoff-contract.md:46:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/FANNAN-PLAN.md:29:### 1. Reconcile the brief and define design success\nrelease/FANNAN-PLAN.md:31:Read the current step from the brief. Freeze a source snapshot with stable brief line IDs, page/template inventory, audience, principal job, conversion or task goal, known constraints and decision status. Resolve repository, stack, design tool, roles and languages from settings. Write observable success criteria for each visitor task. If a brief, rules file, authoritative role or essential fact is missing, record the gap and its owner; do not substitute a guessed fact.\nrelease/FANNAN-PLAN.md:45:Map each page and section to a visitor task and an exact brief line. Each section brief names its purpose, content slots, evidence, CTA and destination, expected state changes and success check. Remove sections with no job. A structural decision, grid break, illustration or motion proposal gets the same trace, so the critic can reject anything without one.\nrelease/FANNAN-PLAN.md:71:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/FANNAN-PLAN.md:127:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/FANNAN-PLAN.md:137:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/FANNAN-PLAN.md:141:All local command results and negative-path checks are in the separate verification record. Anything not executed is in the untested list. Historical test claims stay historical. This candidate does not create Amin's review, live credentials, branch enforcement, provider access, a real approved design or a successful live handoff.\nrelease/references/critic-rubric.md:16:| Typography and language | Deliberate role pairing, at most six sizes, readable measures, correct scripts/directions and uncut translations | Token-to-DOM mapping, language renders, long-text/zoom checks; clipping or missing script support fails |\nrelease/references/critic-rubric.md:18:| Color, imagery and restraint | Legible neutral base, one accent within area budget, useful licensed imagery, no default effects | Measured color roles, contrast, screenshot, asset jobs; palette/card/gradient/glass rule violation fails |\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:5:## Measurement contract\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:9:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:17:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:34:| Accent area | At most 10% full-page and at most 10% reviewed viewport | Declared accent token(s), computed-style proxy, screenshot measurement including accent inside media/effects | Visual |\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:58:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:72:Measure actual pointer targets. A 24 × 24 CSS-pixel target is the baseline; any smaller target needs a documented qualifying spacing, equivalent-control, inline, user-agent or essential exception. Bounding boxes and an “inline” tag are only screening heuristics. [W3C target-size guidance](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/target-size-minimum).\nrelease/references/design-quality.md:76:Check 200% text resizing and 400% desktop zoom/reflow (equivalent 320 CSS-pixel width), including applicable two-dimensional content exceptions. This is accessibility validation, not authorization to design phone layouts. Document browser zoom and viewport used. [W3C reflow guidance](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/reflow.html)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f80f814-38ed-4ed2-80fc-18e1bfbe6740","uuid":"ff00c8ef-fe59-4764-a5d5-612275d146c4","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:27:50.333Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:16:export const states = ['default', 'hover', 'focus', 'disabled', 'empty', 'loading', 'error'];\nrelease/skills/design-ui-map/SKILL.md:6:[Omitted long matching line]\nrelease/skills/design-process/SKILL.md:14:1. **Reconcile brief and success.** Map approved/open/evidence-pending decisions, page inventory, roles, gates, visitor tasks, measurable criteria. Resolve conflicts before exit.\nrelea